=== REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS ===
1. DelegationMutex Fact (Emergency Mutex Relaxation):
   - Refine the fact to explicitly permit a user to hold a mutex pair of roles in Emergency mode only if at least one role is held via delegation (direct assignment of both remains forbidden at all times).
   - Update the DelegationMutex fact as follows:
     ```
     fact DelegationMutex {
         // In all modes, direct assignment of mutex roles is forbidden
         all s: State | all u: User | all r1, r2: Role |
             r2 in r1.mutexWith => not (r1 in directRoles[s, u] and r2 in directRoles[s, u])
         // In Normal mode, mutex roles forbidden (both direct and delegated)
         all s: State | s.mode = Normal =>
             all u: User | all r1, r2: Role |
                 r2 in r1.mutexWith => not (r1 in s.userRoles[u] and r2 in s.userRoles[u])
         // In Emergency mode, mutex roles allowed only if at least one held via delegation
         all s: State | s.mode = Emergency =>
             all u: User | all r1, r2: Role |
                 r2 in r1.mutexWith =>
                     not (r1 in s.userRoles[u] and r2 in s.userRoles[u])
                     or (some d: Delegation | d.to = u and d in s.activeDelegations and (d.role = r1 or d.role = r2))
     }
     ```
   - Rationale: This ensures that in Emergency, mutex roles can be held together only if delegation is involved, matching requirements.

2. Liveness Constraint for Request Processing (All Requests Eventually Processed):
   - Add a liveness fact to guarantee that every request is eventually processed in some Normal mode state.
   - Example addition:
     ```
     fact AllRequestsEventuallyProcessed {
         all r: Request | some s: State | s.mode = Normal and s.reqStatus[r] = Processed
     }
     ```
   - Alternatively, if temporal patterns are needed, ensure that the system cannot reach a dead-end where requests remain perpetually pending.

3. Regression Guard:
   - Ensure that existing passing assertions (assertRoleAssignmentClearance, assertDelegationClearance, etc.) remain stable after implementing the above fixes.

