=== REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS ===
Refine the DelegationMutex fact to enforce the following:

1. In Emergency mode, a user may only hold both of a mutually exclusive role pair if at least one is held via delegation (never both by direct assignment). The current fact permits too much by allowing the case where a user could theoretically hold both via direct assignment if any delegation exists, which is not intended.

2. Update the relevant portion of the DelegationMutex fact as follows (replace the Emergency-mode block only):

Replace:
```
all s: State |
    s.mode = Emergency =>
        all u: User |
            all r1, r2: Role |
                r2 in r1.mutexWith =>
                    not (r1 in s.userRoles[u] and r2 in s.userRoles[u])
                    or (some d: Delegation | d.to = u and d in s.activeDelegations and (d.role = r1 or d.role = r2))
```
With stricter logic:
```
all s: State |
    s.mode = Emergency =>
        all u: User |
            all r1, r2: Role |
                r2 in r1.mutexWith =>
                    // User may hold both mutex roles iff (at least one is via delegation), and never both via direct assignment
                    (r1 in s.userRoles[u] and r2 in s.userRoles[u]) =>
                        ( (some d1: Delegation | d1.to = u and d1.role = r1 and d1 in s.activeDelegations)
                          or
                          (some d2: Delegation | d2.to = u and d2.role = r2 and d2 in s.activeDelegations)
                        )
                        and not (r1 in directRoles[s, u] and r2 in directRoles[s, u])
```
Rationale: This ensures that, in Emergency, a user can only hold both mutex roles if at least one is via delegation, and never both directly—matching the requirement and enabling the assertion to pass.

